  "title": "wslua_dissector: Support 'decode_as' from DissectorTable:try()",
  "description": "When I'm registering a dissector for 'decode as' from a lua dissector\nusing DissectorTable.new(), the code requires me to use ftypes.NONE\nif it ia a pure \"decode as\" dissector, where there's no port number\n/ payload id / protocol id to match on.\n\nHowever, without this patch, calling dissector_table:try() will fail for\nsuch a dissector table, as the code in DissectorTable_try does not\nhandle FT_NONE and will raise \"No such type of dissector table\".\n\nWith the attached patch I'm able to get that working.",
